      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be really awesome to have. I know a lot of people like using qr codes for links since it looks nicer and is easier to fit onto a design and it would be ideal if users could scan from in game easily without having to jump out of vr just to scan the code.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-26T11:46:28.394Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While VRChat is missing web panels, one of the most underrated tools for content creators, as an alternative, I suggest adding a built-in QR scanner to the virtual camera. \nOf course, it can be used not only for links users could potentially scan in order to get redirected to a website using Steam overlay, which should be really comfortable. \nI've seen people use QR codes enough to say this feature could become really useful, and even if you think about it just as a compromise due to the absence of web panels, if they're going to come back eventually, it's going to be even better with the ability to view websites on your in-app screen locally without leaving VRChat.",
